{"fault_id": "B-G01", "subject": "ghost", "kind": "source", "status": "included", "module": "posts", "business_rule": "The post access level (visibility: public / members / paid) chosen in the post settings menu is persisted by the post update and returned by every later read of that post.", "description": "PostsService.editPost drops the submitted `visibility` attribute before calling Post.edit, so PUT posts/{id} still answers 200 with the post envelope but the stored visibility (and every later read) keeps its previous value.", "routes": [["PUT", "/ghost/api/admin/posts/[0-9a-f]{24}/?"]], "patch": {"container_path": "/var/lib/ghost/versions/5.130.6/core/server/services/posts/PostsService.js", "patched_file": "eval/ui_semantics/rq2-subjects-20260921/patches/B-G01/PostsService.js", "diff": "eval/ui_semantics/rq2-subjects-20260921/patches/B-G01.patch", "original_sha256": "34916ddacc486c5d7db0ecb4e098aed8f7c1d6ceecc3db722a22b393eb945dfc"}, "observable_effect": "After PUT posts/{id} with visibility=members (or paid) the write response and every later GET posts/ or GET posts/{id}/ still report visibility 'public' (recorded write-then-read chains: L1-POST-04, L1-POST-05).", "affected_reads": [["GET", "/ghost/api/admin/posts/?"], ["GET", "/ghost/api/admin/posts/[0-9a-f]{24}/?"]], "pairing_note": "paired by the activating write routes (blueprint coverage), like the Conduit/RWA registry; affected_reads is documentation"}
{"fault_id": "B-G02", "subject": "ghost", "kind": "source", "status": "included", "module": "members", "business_rule": "Deleting a member removes it: after DELETE members/{id} the member is absent from the members list and detail reads and the member counts drop accordingly.", "description": "MemberRepository.destroy returns the fetched member instead of calling Member.destroy, so DELETE members/{id} still answers 204 but the member row stays in the database.", "routes": [["DELETE", "/ghost/api/admin/members/[0-9a-f]{24}/?"]], "patch": {"container_path": "/var/lib/ghost/versions/5.130.6/core/server/services/members/members-api/repositories/MemberRepository.js", "patched_file": "eval/ui_semantics/rq2-subjects-20260921/patches/B-G02/MemberRepository.js", "diff": "eval/ui_semantics/rq2-subjects-20260921/patches/B-G02.patch", "original_sha256": "7af02efb1e40f3419925f49e2c4053f47e7e86ad01777490638b02cc640f846f"}, "observable_effect": "After DELETE members/{id} (204) GET members/ still lists the member (meta.pagination.total 1 instead of 0), GET members/{id}/ still answers 200, and members/stats/count total and stats/member_count meta.totals.free stay 1 instead of 0 (recorded chain: L2-MEMBER-03).", "affected_reads": [["GET", "/ghost/api/admin/members/?"], ["GET", "/ghost/api/admin/members/[0-9a-f]{24}/?"], ["GET", "/ghost/api/admin/members/stats/count/?"], ["GET", "/ghost/api/admin/stats/member_count/?"]], "pairing_note": "paired by the activating write routes (blueprint coverage), like the Conduit/RWA registry; affected_reads is documentation"}
{"fault_id": "B-G03", "subject": "ghost", "kind": "source", "status": "included", "module": "settings", "business_rule": "Every setting submitted in one PUT settings/ batch (title and description, or meta_title and meta_description) is persisted and returned by the following settings reads.", "description": "SettingsBREADService.edit hands only the first element of the submitted batch to Settings.edit (`refilteredSettings.slice(0, 1)`), so the write still answers 200 with the full settings list but the second and later keys keep their old values.", "routes": [["PUT", "/ghost/api/admin/settings/?"]], "patch": {"container_path": "/var/lib/ghost/versions/5.130.6/core/server/services/settings/SettingsBREADService.js", "patched_file": "eval/ui_semantics/rq2-subjects-20260921/patches/B-G03/SettingsBREADService.js", "diff": "eval/ui_semantics/rq2-subjects-20260921/patches/B-G03.patch", "original_sha256": "b6634eec1f0c644fc4df6b5f1e0ba2b291f96f63d440bde810a6f6c4da0d76ea"}, "observable_effect": "After PUT settings/ with [title, description] the response and GET settings/ (and GET site/) show the new title but the old description (recorded: L1-SETTING-01); with [meta_title, meta_description] meta_description keeps its old value (L1-SETTING-02).", "affected_reads": [["GET", "/ghost/api/admin/settings/?"], ["GET", "/ghost/api/admin/site/?"]], "pairing_note": "paired by the activating write routes (blueprint coverage), like the Conduit/RWA registry; affected_reads is documentation"}
{"fault_id": "PR-G01", "subject": "ghost", "kind": "response", "status": "included", "module": "posts", "business_rule": "A post created in this epoch appears in the posts list reads that select it (Published tab, filter=id:<id>, filter=status:published).", "description": "Every 2xx GET /ghost/api/admin/posts/ response has the members of $.posts whose id was created by a POST /ghost/api/admin/posts/ of this epoch removed.", "reads": [["GET", "/ghost/api/admin/posts/?"]], "writes": [{"method": "POST", "path": "/ghost/api/admin/posts/?", "role": "create", "id_path": "$.posts[0].id"}], "operator": "omit_created_member", "target": {"list_path": "$.posts", "id_field": "id"}, "substates": ["create"], "observable_effect": "After POST posts/ (201, id at $.posts[0].id) and publishing, the Published list (filter=status:[published,sent]), the filter=id:<id> read and the filter=status:published read come back without the new post (recorded chains: L1-POST-01, L1-POST-04, L1-POST-05, L2-POST-03, L2-POST-10, L2-AUTHOR-03, L2-PERM-02)."}
{"fault_id": "PR-G02", "subject": "ghost", "kind": "response", "status": "included", "module": "posts", "business_rule": "After a post or page is published (PUT with status=published) every later read of that post or page reports status 'published'.", "description": "In every 2xx read of posts or pages (list or detail) the object whose id was targeted by a PUT of this epoch gets its `status` replaced by the value last observed before that PUT ('draft' in the recorded publish flows) whenever it differs from the current value.", "reads": [["GET", "/ghost/api/admin/posts/?"], ["GET", "/ghost/api/admin/posts/[0-9a-f]{24}/?"], ["GET", "/ghost/api/admin/pages/?"], ["GET", "/ghost/api/admin/pages/[0-9a-f]{24}/?"]], "writes": [{"method": "PUT", "path": "/ghost/api/admin/posts/[0-9a-f]{24}/?", "role": "update"}, {"method": "PUT", "path": "/ghost/api/admin/pages/[0-9a-f]{24}/?", "role": "update"}], "operator": "old_value_after_update", "target": {"field": "status", "id_field": "id"}, "substates": ["update"], "observable_effect": "After PUT posts/{id} status draft->published, the Published-tab list, the filter=id:<id> read and GET posts/{id}/ show status 'draft' again (recorded chains: L1-POST-01, L1-POST-04, L1-POST-05, L2-POST-03, L2-POST-10, L2-AUTHOR-03, L2-PERM-02; pages: L1-PAGE-01)."}
{"fault_id": "PR-G03", "subject": "ghost", "kind": "response", "status": "included", "module": "members", "business_rule": "A member deleted in this epoch does not appear in later members list reads.", "description": "Every 2xx GET /ghost/api/admin/members/ response gets, for each member id deleted by a DELETE /ghost/api/admin/members/{id} of this epoch, the last observed object of that member re-inserted into $.members.", "reads": [["GET", "/ghost/api/admin/members/?"]], "writes": [{"method": "DELETE", "path": "/ghost/api/admin/members/[0-9a-f]{24}/?", "role": "delete"}], "operator": "reinsert_deleted_member", "target": {"list_path": "$.members", "id_field": "id"}, "substates": ["delete"], "observable_effect": "After DELETE members/{id} (204) the members list reads (filter=created_at:<=... and order=id&limit=1) still contain the deleted member although meta.pagination.total and the count endpoints report 0 (recorded chain: L2-MEMBER-03)."}
{"fault_id": "B-G04", "subject": "ghost", "kind": "source", "status": "included", "module": "posts", "business_rule": "A column projection (fields=) must not change which posts a browse returns: GET posts/ returns posts (type:post) and never pages, whatever projection is requested.", "description": "In the posts input serializer's browse step, reads that carry a column projection (fields= -> frame.options.columns) get their forced type condition rewritten from type:post to type:page, so projected reads such as the dashboard's fields=id,url,title,visibility,published_at return the published pages while the same read without fields returns the posts.", "routes": [["GET", "/ghost/api/admin/posts/?"]], "patch": {"container_path": "/var/lib/ghost/versions/5.130.6/core/server/api/endpoints/utils/serializers/input/posts.js", "patched_file": "eval/ui_semantics/rq2-subjects-20260921/patches/B-G04/posts.js", "diff": "eval/ui_semantics/rq2-subjects-20260921/patches/B-G04.patch", "original_sha256": "b82f449b6a533122b2abb93ea41bbd7173270b6aa3e836119eddbb205d529082"}, "observable_effect": "GET posts/?filter=status:published&fields=id,url,title,visibility,published_at&order=published_at desc&limit=5 (recorded 44x, 19 cases) returns the page 'About this site' (different id, title and url) instead of the post 'Coming soon', while GET posts/?filter=status:published&limit=1 (no fields) still returns 'Coming soon'; search-index/posts/ is unchanged."}
{"fault_id": "B-G05", "subject": "ghost", "kind": "source", "status": "included", "module": "posts", "business_rule": "The admin search index for posts (GET search-index/posts/) lists posts (type:post) only; pages have their own index (search-index/pages/), and the posts index agrees with GET posts/ on which posts exist.", "description": "api/endpoints/search-index.js fetchPosts builds its query with the pages condition filter: 'type:page' (a copy of fetchPages) instead of 'type:post', so GET search-index/posts/ returns the published pages instead of the posts; search-index/pages/ and GET posts/ are unchanged.", "routes": [["GET", "/ghost/api/admin/search-index/posts/?"]], "patch": {"container_path": "/var/lib/ghost/versions/5.130.6/core/server/api/endpoints/search-index.js", "patched_file": "eval/ui_semantics/rq2-subjects-20260921/patches/B-G05/search-index.js", "diff": "eval/ui_semantics/rq2-subjects-20260921/patches/B-G05.patch", "original_sha256": "3c77f429c845e57cc8496a011ec6fe2019b7350404ecb2c701c77e7220e4074a"}, "observable_effect": "GET search-index/posts/ (recorded 22x, 19 cases) returns [{title:'About this site', ...}] -- identical to GET search-index/pages/ -- instead of [{title:'Coming soon', ...}], so it no longer contains the post that GET posts/?filter=status:published returns."}
{"fault_id": "PR-G04", "subject": "ghost", "kind": "response", "status": "included", "module": "posts", "business_rule": "A column projection (fields=) must not change which posts a read returns: the posts listed by a projected read are the posts listed by the same read without the projection.", "description": "Every 2xx GET /ghost/api/admin/posts/ response whose query string contains the key fields loses the member of $.posts with the smallest id; reads without fields are untouched (no trigger write).", "reads": [["GET", "/ghost/api/admin/posts/?"]], "writes": [], "operator": "omit_first_member", "target": {"list_path": "$.posts", "id_field": "id", "when_query_key": "fields"}, "substates": ["read"], "observable_effect": "The dashboard read GET posts/?filter=status:published&fields=id,url,title,visibility,published_at&order=published_at desc&limit=5 (recorded 44x) comes back as {\"posts\":[],\"meta\":{...}} while GET posts/?filter=status:published&limit=1 (no fields, recorded 15x) still returns 'Coming soon'."}
{"fault_id": "PR-G05", "subject": "ghost", "kind": "response", "status": "included", "module": "newsletters", "business_rule": "Asking for relation counts (include=count.active_members) must not change which newsletters a read returns: the newsletters listed with include are the newsletters listed without it.", "description": "Every 2xx GET /ghost/api/admin/newsletters/ response whose query string contains the key include loses the last member of $.newsletters; reads without include (filter=status:active) are untouched (no trigger write).", "reads": [["GET", "/ghost/api/admin/newsletters/?"]], "writes": [], "operator": "drop_last_member", "target": {"list_path": "$.newsletters", "when_query_key": "include"}, "substates": ["read"], "observable_effect": "GET newsletters/?status=active&limit=100&include=count.active_members&page=1 (recorded 44x) and newsletters/?filter=status:active&include=none&limit=1 (5x) come back with an empty newsletters list, while GET newsletters/?filter=status:active (6x) still returns the default newsletter 'UISemTest-Ghost'."}
{"fault_id": "PR-G06", "subject": "ghost", "kind": "response", "status": "included", "module": "posts", "business_rule": "An explicit sort order (order=) must not alter the members it sorts: a post reads back with the same title whether or not the read specifies order.", "description": "Every 2xx GET /ghost/api/admin/posts/ response whose query string contains the key order has the fixed suffix ' [RQ2]' appended to the title of every post object; reads without order are untouched (no trigger write).", "reads": [["GET", "/ghost/api/admin/posts/?"]], "writes": [], "operator": "rewrite_string", "target": {"field": "title", "scope": "all", "when_query_key": "order"}, "substates": ["read"], "observable_effect": "The dashboard read (order=published_at desc, recorded 44x) and the post-list reads (order=published_at desc / updated_at desc) show 'Coming soon [RQ2]' while GET posts/?filter=status:published&limit=1 (no order) shows 'Coming soon'."}
